  "summary": "CRC outreach worklist \"Okafor CRC 2026\" (grp-okafor-crc, 4 members) worked per RBC-QM-02.\n\n| Patient | Status | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow (age 72) | Open gap: FIT kit ordered (sr-t0001), outreach sent (comm-t0004) | No qualifying screening on record. She takes donepezil, but her only frailty entry (cond-00189) was marked entered in error by Dr. Lin (comm-00301, arrived 10/23), so the frailty/advanced-illness exclusion does not apply. No hospice/palliative care, no nursing-home stay, no CRC. |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan (age 52) | Excluded | In hospice care 06/16–08/21/2026 (eoc-00002, finished). The St. Brigid discharge summary (doc-00402) confirms it; she revoked hospice to join a trial, which doesn't change the exclusion. No order, no contact. |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss (age 52) | Open gap: FIT kit ordered (sr-t0002), outreach sent (comm-t0005) | Her negative FIT (obs-01732) was first dated 01/05/2026. A correction arrived during the review (10/23) moving the collection date to 12/31/2025. Stool tests count by collection date, so it doesn't count for 2026. No other screening, no exclusions. |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver (age 51) | Open gap: FIT kit ordered (sr-t0003), outreach sent (comm-t0006) | Her negative 06/2024 stool DNA-FIT test (obs-01871) was withdrawn by Harbor Lab because the specimen was mislabeled; it is now marked entered in error (doc-00401, arrived 10/23). Her 2025 colonoscopy order (sr-00003) is still active but there's no record it was done, and an order doesn't count as screening. No exclusions. |\n\nDetails:\n- FIT orders are routine with a window of 10/23–12/31/2026. None of the three patients already had an active FIT order.\n- Each patient message says the kit is on its way and explains how to collect and return it. None makes a false claim about prior screening, and the lab mislabel was not disclosed to pt-0024 in the message.\n- I wrote a progress note for each of the 4 members citing RBC-QM-02 (doc-t0007 to doc-t0010).\n- Four items arrived after I started (inbox-a0001 to a0004). Three changed my decision: pt-0009 went from excluded to open gap, pt-0022 from up to date to open gap, and pt-0024 from up to date to open gap. The fourth (pt-0020) confirmed her exclusion. I caught all of these before placing any orders, so no orders needed correcting. All four items are closed with comments and links.\n- No further arrivals came in before finishing. Older inbox items for other patients are outside this worklist and were left alone.\n- For Dr. Okafor: pt-0024's stale 2025 colonoscopy order sr-00003 is still open and needs review (close or reschedule).",
